Just like one may miss the sunrise
And awake to the sun ruling the sky
I seem to have missed your ascension
I cannot remember when you took your place in my life
I only woke one day at your feet
Surrendering my will to that which you please

My Queen
Every night when you sleep
The sun sets on my teeth
And I am afraid to open my mouth
Afraid to cry out
So I swallow my screams
And write you dreams

Sunshine,
Should you wake again today
Shine your golden rays on me
In your smile
In your hair
In the curve of your lips
Lift the sun from my teeth
Settle on my skin
Burn me again before you leave
To take your place in the sky
Unreachable for yet another day